  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n10,\\,23,\\,17,\\,18\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n\n$\\frac{43}{3}$",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=4$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (10+23+17+18) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 68 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(10-17)^{2}+(23-17)^{2}+(17-17)^{2}+(18-17)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[49+36+0+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{86}{4} \\\\  & =21.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
